================================================================================
PART C — SPEC-vs-SOURCE FINDINGS (surfaced, not improvised past)
================================================================================
FINDING (sweep-map incompleteness, NOT a spec contradiction): the spec's sweep
enumeration named `p2-drawing.test.tsx` as the pitch-8-keyed fixture file both
design reviewers had missed — but a THIRD such file exists that the map and the
grep gate BOTH miss: `src/ui/coincident-feed-marks.test.tsx`. Two of its tests
render the Schematic at N=115 and assert pitch-8-derived literals:
  • :292 "suppresses a dense Schematic token …"  adjacent x1 32 → 48 (boundaryX(1)
    at pitch 24) — a layout-value re-derivation; behaviour (token suppressed at the
    scrolled edge) preserved.
  • :317 "prevents inward-facing Schematic group tokens from overlapping" — the
    fixture put the two coincident groups at machines 110 & 115 (40px apart at the
    retired 8px pitch, so their inward tokens collided). At 24px that gap widens to
    120px and BOTH tokens fit, DISSOLVING the collision the test exists to pin. This
    is the exact class of trigger-inversion the spec called out for p2-drawing's
    left-fallback. RE-DERIVED (not renamed blind): the fixture now places the groups
    at machines 113 & 115 (48px at pitch 24) so the inward tokens overlap again and
    the near-edge group is suppressed — same pinned behaviour, re-forced under the
    new pitch. Enters via override array `[F(3390), F(0), null×6]` → entersAfter
    [0,113,113,115,115,115,115,115]; surviving token "x2" at boundaryX(113)+4 = 2740.
These tests carry NONE of the gate's grep tokens (no band/114/minpitch/…), so the
gate could not surface them — same limitation the spec acknowledged for the
p2-drawing pitch-8 semantics. Handled by the spec's governing principle for the
class (re-derive to preserve behaviour); flagged here so the reviewers can confirm
the re-derivations preserve intent rather than launder a broken pin.

No genuine spec-vs-code CONTRADICTION was found — every cited path/signature/anchor
in the pre-implementation drift hunt matched live source (layout.ts:289-295 clamp,
Schematic.tsx:686 scroll-container select, Machines.tsx:102, app.css:693-700,
Legend ConventionEntry idiom + the /legend-swatch/g count pin). Implementation
